From: SwiftPili <359733720+haikiseven@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: native AV1 hardware decode (fixes F17 black)

AV1 was decoded through a custom FFmpeg-VA module (va_videotoolbox.c) whose
`get` op captured frame->data[3] at get_buffer2 time -- BEFORE decode.
VideoToolbox's AV1 decoder allocates its OWN output CVPixelBuffer and FFmpeg
swaps it into data[3] AFTER decode, so the captured pool buffer stayed empty and
the picture rendered black (design doc F17). The module clones the frame at
get-time, freezing the pre-decode pointers, and there is no post-decode VA hook
-- so it cannot be fixed in that module.

The native VideoToolbox decoder owns its VTDecompressionSession and receives the
decoded CVPixelBuffer directly, exactly as it does for H.264/HEVC (which render
fine). Teach it AV1. Like MP4V it is a "non-parsed" codec: the container supplies
the PTS (output ordering), the picture size, and the av1C config, so no per-codec
parsing/reorder callbacks are needed -- only pf_copy_extradata, wrapping the av1C
record as the format-description atom. At capability 800 this module is tried
before avcodec, so AV1 now takes the native path. A device without AV1 hardware
decode is rejected up front (VTIsHardwareDecodeSupported), and VLC falls back to
avcodec/dav1d exactly as before.

Targets VLC c833c4be0 (modules/codec/videotoolbox/decoder.c).

diff --git a/modules/codec/videotoolbox/decoder.c b/modules/codec/videotoolbox/decoder.c
--- a/modules/codec/videotoolbox/decoder.c
+++ b/modules/codec/videotoolbox/decoder.c
@@ -796,5 +796,17 @@
     else
         return NULL; /* MPEG4 without esds ? */
 }
+
+static CFDictionaryRef CopyDecoderExtradataAV1(decoder_t *p_dec)
+{
+    /* The av1C record (AV1CodecConfigurationRecord) is the whole config; the
+     * mp4 demuxer hands it over as p_extra. VideoToolbox reads it from the
+     * "av1C" atom under SampleDescriptionExtensionAtoms, like h264's avcC. */
+    if (p_dec->fmt_in->i_extra)
+        return ExtradataInfoCreate(CFSTR("av1C"), p_dec->fmt_in->p_extra,
+                                                  p_dec->fmt_in->i_extra);
+    else
+        return NULL;
+}
 
 /* !Codec Specific */
@@ -930,3 +930,14 @@
             return kCMVideoCodecType_HEVC;
+
+        case VLC_CODEC_AV1:
+            /* Native VideoToolbox AV1 -- bypasses the FFmpeg-VA path whose
+             * pre-decode buffer capture rendered AV1 black (design doc F17). */
+            if (!VTIsHardwareDecodeSupported(kCMVideoCodecType_AV1))
+            {
+                msg_Warn(p_dec, "device doesn't support AV1");
+                return 0;
+            }
+            msg_Dbg(p_dec, "using native VideoToolbox AV1 decode");
+            return kCMVideoCodecType_AV1;
 
         case VLC_CODEC_MP4V:
@@ -1420,5 +1420,9 @@
         case kCMVideoCodecType_MPEG4Video:
             p_sys->pf_copy_extradata = CopyDecoderExtradataMPEG4;
             break;
+
+        case kCMVideoCodecType_AV1:
+            p_sys->pf_copy_extradata = CopyDecoderExtradataAV1;
+            break;
 
         default:
